---
// Astro returns BASE_URL without a trailing slash at the root but with one
// under a subpath; normalise so `${base}x` is never `/cyber-cvx`.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Stat from '../components/Stat.astro';
import BarList from '../components/BarList.astro';
import { qdrant, qdrantTotal, graphs, rules, capturedAt } from '../data/hive';
import { teamBrain } from '../data/team-brain';
import { claudeStatement, references } from '../data/references';
import { teamBrainSystem, factoriumSystem } from '../data/systems';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';

---
<Base
  title="Michal Malček — AI Engineer, Integrator, Explorer"
  description="AI engineer. One production system delivered and handed over, one running daily — built and measured on a single local machine."
>
  <header class="relative pt-20 pb-10">
    <span class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-px pointer-events-none"
          style="background: linear-gradient(90deg,
                   color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-neural) 65%, transparent) 0%,
                   color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-synapse) 35%, transparent) 35%,
                   var(--color-line) 75%, transparent 100%);
                 box-shadow: 0 0 16px -2px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-neural) 55%, transparent)" />
    <div class="status-pill inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] tracking-[.14em] uppercase
                text-synapse border border-synapse rounded-full px-3 py-1 mb-5">
      <span class="w-[6px] h-[6px] rounded-full bg-synapse" style="animation: pulse 2.4s ease-in-out infinite" />
      Open to AI research engineering roles
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-[clamp(34px,6vw,58px)] leading-[1.04] font-semibold tracking-tight m-0 mb-3">
      <span class="glow-name">Michal Malček</span><br /><em
        class="not-italic text-neural-text glow-violet">AI Engineer, Integrator, Explorer</em>
    </h1>

    <!-- The theme song. A CV with a soundtrack is a claim about attitude, so the
         line explains the connection rather than leaving it as a gag. -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-6">
      <a href="https://suno.com/s/CgpdUedfU3jqZBCI" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
         class="play-btn group inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 no-underline rounded-full
                pl-2 pr-4 py-1.5 border border-neural/45 text-[13px]">
        <span class="play-disc inline-flex items-center justify-center w-[26px] h-[26px] rounded-full shrink-0">
          <svg width="9" height="11" viewBox="0 0 9 11" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M0 0.5L9 5.5L0 10.5V0.5Z" fill="currentColor" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="text-fg font-semibold tracking-tight">Cyber Junglist</span>
        <span class="text-fg-ghost text-[11.5px]">theme song</span>
      </a>
      <span class="text-[11.5px] text-fg-ghost">drum &amp; bass · jungle · rave</span>
    </div>

    <p class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost max-w-[620px] m-0 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
      This cyber CV tastes best with its theme song, made for exactly this purpose.{' '}
      <span class="text-fg-dim">Jungle and cybernetics have shared a vocabulary since the
      early nineties — feedback, breaks, systems that reorganise themselves under load — so a
      CV about building one may as well arrive with a breakbeat.</span> More of the
      cyberpunk neuro-DnB experiments: <a href="https://suno.com/@miso_m" target="_blank"
      rel="noopener" class="no-underline hover:underline">suno.com/@miso_m</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="text-[clamp(15px,2vw,18px)] text-fg-dim max-w-[640px] m-0 mb-7">
      Twenty years across both sides of software delivery — ERP testing at nineteen, Google
      in Prague and Dublin at twenty-four, eight years proving things with measurement in a
      market that punishes wishful thinking. In the last year that turned into AI engineering:
      <b class="text-fg">one production system delivered and handed over, one running daily on
      the machine under my desk.</b> No AI degree — one three-day course, then everything else
      learned from the systems themselves.
    </p>

    <Contact />
  </header>



  <!-- ── What is here ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section id="map" title="What is here" note="five ways in">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3">

      <a href={`${base}career/`} class="card p-5 no-underline flex flex-col group">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Career</span>
          <span class="text-fg-ghost text-[15px] leading-none transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[14px] text-fg mb-3">Twenty years, both sides of delivery</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-3">
          {[['14', 'ERP implementations sold'], ['30k', 'monthly sessions built from zero'],
            ['4', 'AI workshops for a whole branch']].map(([v, l]) => (
            <div>
              <div class="text-[17px] font-semibold lit-forge leading-none">{v}</div>
              <div class="text-[10.5px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug mt-1">{l}</div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-dim m-0 flex-1">
          Asseco at 19 · Google Prague and Dublin at 24 · eight years of organic growth in a
          market that punishes guessing · then AI, by building rather than by title.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href={`${base}systems/`} class="card p-5 no-underline flex flex-col group">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Systems</span>
          <span class="text-fg-ghost text-[15px] leading-none transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[14px] text-fg mb-3">Two, and they are not the same thing</div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 mb-3">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2.5 text-[12.5px]">
            <b class="text-forge shrink-0 w-[86px]">Team Brain</b>
            <span class="text-fg-dim">5 data sources · 33 tools · 15 users · <b class="text-fg">93.9%</b> tool success over 1,352 calls</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2.5 text-[12.5px]">
            <b class="text-synapse shrink-0 w-[86px]">Factorium</b>
            <span class="text-fg-dim">one 24&nbsp;GB machine · two models · <b class="text-fg">no cloud inference</b> · 60 tools, 22 visible per turn</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-dim m-0 flex-1">
          A multi-source analytics platform a team used daily, and a local-first environment
          where a person and two models share one memory. Plus what went wrong in both.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href={`${base}research/`} class="card p-5 no-underline flex flex-col group md:col-span-2">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Research</span>
          <span class="text-fg-ghost text-[15px] leading-none transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[14px] text-fg mb-3">Three findings I would defend in a room</div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-3">
          {[
            ['1 in 5 → 10/10', 'Rules stored as their own wording could not be found from the situation they govern. Stored as descriptions of those situations, retrieval went to ten out of ten — and the top-5 spread of 2.4% proved it was never a ranking problem.'],
            ['7 of 8 misjudged', 'Asked which of its own rules carried real information, the model got seven of eight wrong — including three that had changed its behaviour minutes earlier. A model can follow a rule without being able to judge one.'],
            ['1,512 of 3,039', 'Entities silently lost their centrality tier after one ordinary session. A derived global property is a cache, and a null tier reads as "unimportant" when it means "not measured".'],
          ].map(([v, l]) => (
            <div class="border-l-2 border-neural/40 pl-3">
              <div class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-fg leading-tight mb-1.5">{v}</div>
              <p class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug m-0">{l}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-dim m-0">
          Two studies and a technical report, written from stored records rather than
          recollection — including the seven designs that were rejected on evidence, and the
          conclusion of mine that turned out to be wrong.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href={`${base}crystal/`} class="card p-5 no-underline flex flex-col group">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">The crystal</span>
          <span class="text-fg-ghost text-[15px] leading-none transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[14px] text-fg mb-3">The graph, in three dimensions</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-3">
          {[[graphs.knowledge.entities.toLocaleString('en-US'), 'entities'],
            [graphs.knowledge.relationships.toLocaleString('en-US'), 'relationships'],
            [qdrantTotal.toLocaleString('en-US'), 'embedded points']].map(([v, l]) => (
            <div>
              <div class="text-[17px] font-semibold lit-cyan leading-none">{v}</div>
              <div class="text-[10.5px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug mt-1">{l}</div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-dim m-0 flex-1">
          Entities positioned by their real degree and centrality tier, not by hand. Click one
          and it tells you what it connects to and how much of that lies outside the view.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a href={`${base}credentials/`} class="card p-5 no-underline flex flex-col group">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Credentials</span>
          <span class="text-fg-ghost text-[15px] leading-none transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[14px] text-fg mb-3">Checked, not claimed</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-3">
          {[['1.0 – 1.7', 'grade averages'], ['13,270', 'views, papers from 2011'],
            ['2011', 'a reference from Google']].map(([v, l]) => (
            <div>
              <div class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-fg leading-none">{v}</div>
              <div class="text-[10.5px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug mt-1">{l}</div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-dim m-0 flex-1">
          Every source link probed rather than assumed — five turned out to be login walls and
          three had gone offline in the years since. Those say so instead of pretending.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ── The hive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section
    id="hive"
    title="The hive, in numbers"
    note={`read ${capturedAt}`}
    lede="Factorium's stores as they stand right now — one person, one machine, no team and no budget. Read live from Postgres and Qdrant by a script rather than typed in, because a number you cannot re-derive is a claim, not a measurement."
  >
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-fg-ghost -mt-2 mb-5">
      <span class="relative inline-flex w-[7px] h-[7px]">
        <span class="absolute inset-0 rounded-full bg-synapse"
              style="box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--color-synapse), 0 0 22px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-synapse) 60%, transparent)" />
        <span class="absolute inset-0 rounded-full bg-synapse"
              style="animation: ripple 2.6s ease-out infinite" />
      </span>
      running while you read this
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-6 gap-3">
      <Stat label="Embedded points" value={qdrantTotal.toLocaleString('en-US')} accent="forge" span={3} delay={0}
            sub="Across seven Qdrant collections at 1024 dimensions.">
        <div class="mt-4"><BarList rows={qdrant} /></div>
      </Stat>

      <Stat label="Knowledge graph" value={graphs.knowledge.entities.toLocaleString('en-US')} accent="neural" span={3} delay={80}
            sub={`entities · <b>${graphs.knowledge.relationships.toLocaleString('en-US')}</b> relationships<br><span class="text-fg-ghost">106 decisions · 283 lessons · 608 concepts</span>`}>
        <div class="relative h-[74px] mt-3 opacity-85">
          {[[8,56,0],[26,22,.9],[41,68,1.9],[58,34,.5],[73,60,2.6],[89,28,1.4]].map(([l,t,d]) => (
            <span class="absolute w-[5px] h-[5px] rounded-full bg-synapse"
                  style={`left:${l}%; top:${t}%;
                          box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--color-synapse),
                                      0 0 20px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-synapse) 70%, transparent),
                                      0 0 40px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-synapse) 35%, transparent);
                          animation: drift 7s ease-in-out ${d}s infinite`} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </Stat>

      <Stat label="Code graph" value={graphs.code.entities.toLocaleString('en-US')} accent="synapse" span={2} delay={160}
            sub={`entities · <b>${graphs.code.relationships.toLocaleString('en-US')}</b> relationships<br><span class="text-fg-ghost">import edges resolved through NodeNext, so blast radius is transitive — 36 files at depth 1, 52 at depth 2, in 34&nbsp;ms</span>`} />

      <Stat label="Living plan" value={graphs.plan.nodes.toLocaleString('en-US')} span={2} delay={240}
            sub={`plan nodes · ${graphs.plan.edges} edges across ${graphs.plan.projects} projects — the plan is a graph in the same database, not a document.`} />

      <Stat label="Behavioural rules" value={rules.rules} span={2} delay={320}
            sub={`rules · ${rules.triggers} situational triggers · defeasible, with overrides logged as data rather than treated as violations.`} />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ── Results ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section
    id="results"
    title="Results"
    lede="Numbers I can point at, across twenty years. Where something is unverifiable or ended badly, it says so."
  >
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-6">
      {[
        { k: 'Traffic built from zero', v: '30k / 100k', s: 'monthly sessions, main site and satellites — German market, no paid links', a: 'forge' },
        { k: 'ERP implementations sold', v: '14', s: 'including EN negotiations with German and Polish pilot customers', a: 'neural' },
        { k: 'First-year turnover', v: '€50k', s: 'monthly, CEE e-commerce business I co-founded', a: 'synapse' },
        { k: 'Tool-call success rate', v: '93.9%', s: 'over 1,352 real calls by non-engineers, four months in production', a: 'forge' },
        { k: 'Direct-mail campaign', v: 'Top 3', s: 'globally at Google by signup rate — the first targeted one for CZ/SK', a: 'neural' },
        { k: 'Judo', v: '3×', s: 'Slovak champion · two years in national representation · ten years training', a: 'synapse' },
      ].map((r, i) => (
        <Stat label={r.k} value={r.v} sub={r.s} accent={r.a as any} delay={i * 60} />
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="card p-5">
      <div class="eyebrow mb-4">Academic record</div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-3">
        {[
          ['Electrical Engineering & ICT — final year', '1.0', 'High School of Jozef Murgaš, Banská Bystrica'],
          ['Information Systems & Technologies (Master\'s, 41 ECTS)', '1.5', 'University of Economics Prague'],
          ['Applied Informatics (Bachelor\'s)', '1.6', 'University of Economics Prague — top 10 of ~500'],
          ['CEMS International Management (Master\'s, in English)', '1.7', 'Prague · Corvinus Budapest'],
        ].map(([what, grade, where]) => (
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 border-b border-line/60 pb-2.5">
            <span class="text-[22px] font-semibold text-forge tabular-nums leading-none shrink-0 w-[38px]">{grade}</span>
            <span>
              <b class="block text-[13px] font-medium leading-snug">{what}</b>
              <span class="text-[11.5px] text-fg-ghost">{where}</span>
            </span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-ghost mt-4 mb-0">
        Czech grading, where 1.0 is the best possible mark. Erasmus at Corvinus Budapest: A in every
        subject. The one I did not finish: the second business-language exam (Russian) in the CEMS
        programme — all mandatory courses and skill seminars completed, that exam not passed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>



  <!-- ── Research ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section id="research" title="Research" note="2 studies · 1 report">
    <div class="card p-6 mb-4">
      <h3 class="text-[19px] font-semibold m-0 mb-1">Measuring whether behavioural rules change model decisions</h3>
      <div class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost mb-3">12 rounds · two models · August 2026</div>
      <p class="text-fg-dim m-0 mb-3">
        Rules for LLM agents are usually written, stored and assumed to work. I measured whether
        mine do, across three questions that normally get conflated: can a rule be
        <em>retrieved</em>, does it <em>change</em> a decision, and does the model <em>know</em>
        which of its rules help it.
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 my-4">
        {[
          ['1 in 5 → 10/10', 'retrieval, once rules were stored as the situations they govern rather than as their own wording'],
          ['6 of 16', 'rules measurably changed a decision · 10 changed nothing · none made a decision worse'],
          ['7 of 8', 'misclassified by the model when asked which of its own rules carried real information'],
        ].map(([v, l]) => (
          <div class="border-l-2 border-neural/40 pl-3">
            <div class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-fg leading-tight">{v}</div>
            <div class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug mt-1">{l}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-fg-dim m-0 mb-3">
        <b>A model can follow a rule without being able to judge one.</b> Three of the rules it
        dismissed as "just advice" had changed its own behaviour minutes earlier. Rule value has to
        be measured behaviourally, never by asking — had I trusted the self-report, I would have
        deleted seven working rules.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[13px] text-fg-ghost m-0 mb-4">
        Seven candidate designs were rejected on evidence: prompt-resident rules, rules in the
        existing graph (top-K collapse), score thresholding, automatic contradiction detection,
        a background guard (254 false alarms per true positive), per-rule hooks, and a solver layer.
      </p>

      <div class="border-t border-line/60 pt-4">
        <div class="text-[10.5px] tracking-[.14em] uppercase text-fg-ghost mb-3">
          Deployed · read from the database, not recalled
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-3">
          {[
            [rules.rules, 'rules'],
            [rules.triggers, 'situational triggers'],
            ['5', 'carry an <i>unless</i> clause'],
            ['2', 'trigger hits so far'],
          ].map(([v, l]) => (
            <div>
              <div class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-fg leading-none">{v}</div>
              <div class="text-[11px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug mt-1" set:html={l} />
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-ghost m-0">
          Two hits is not adoption — but the counter moved off zero on its own, and both firings
          were the class the design predicted: <i>"a health check reports green but the function does
          not work"</i> and <i>"you are claiming a result without fresh evidence."</i>
          <b class="text-fg-dim">The counter itself was broken for part of the study</b> and
          reported a zero that was an unasked question rather than a measurement — the same failure
          class the research is about, occurring inside it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href={`${base}research/rules/`} class="chip no-underline mt-4 inline-block hover:border-neural transition-colors">
        Read the full study →
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-6 mb-4">
      <h3 class="text-[19px] font-semibold m-0 mb-1">Where a node sits should mean something</h3>
      <div class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost mb-3">Spatial metadata · two graphs · July–August 2026</div>
      <p class="text-fg-dim m-0 mb-3">
        Our knowledge graph imploded: the more connected an entity was, the further toward the
        centre it was pulled, so the interesting part collapsed into an unreadable core. Fixing that
        turned into a question worth asking — <b>can a node's position carry information a model can
        read, not just a picture a human can look at?</b>
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 my-4">
        {[
          ['degree-scaled repulsion', 'the standard fix for hub implosion — correct the term that is wrong rather than add a force fighting the springs'],
          ['tokens, not floats', 'a transformer matches strings, it does not compute square roots. Position becomes a discrete tier and cluster label'],
          ['1,512 of 3,039', 'entities silently lost their tier after one session — a derived global property is a cache, and every cache needs an invalidation story'],
        ].map(([v, l]) => (
          <div class="border-l-2 border-synapse/40 pl-3">
            <div class="text-[14px] font-semibold text-fg leading-tight">{v}</div>
            <div class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost leading-snug mt-1">{l}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-fg-dim m-0 mb-3">
        Deployed on both graphs: every entity carries a stored tier and cluster, exposed through
        every read path. The human flies the structure; the model filters on it. Asked directly, the
        local model called it <i>"a global heuristic to prioritise search space and identify
        structural anomalies without exhaustive traversal"</i> — and named the two fields it wanted
        before they were proposed to it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[13px] text-fg-ghost m-0">
        <b class="text-fg-dim">What is not proven, and the paper says so:</b> whether the model's
        reasoning is measurably better with the fields than without them. It says they help and it
        uses them — but the rules study above is exactly why a model's self-report is not evidence.
        That A/B is the experiment this work still owes.
      </p>
      <a href={`${base}research/spatial/`} class="chip no-underline mt-4 inline-block hover:border-neural transition-colors">
        Read the full study →
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-6">
      <h3 class="text-[19px] font-semibold m-0 mb-1">AI engineering — systems, decisions, and what they cost</h3>
      <div class="text-[12px] text-fg-ghost mb-3">Technical report, not research · two systems · stack decisions and their corrections</div>
      <p class="text-fg-dim m-0 mb-3">
        The architecture behind both systems and the reasoning that produced it: one database
        instead of three, a migration of 17,109 vectors and what it bought, a 12B model chosen over
        a stronger 26B, and no agent framework — because a framework that injects prompt content
        you cannot see is fatal when you are measuring how a small model behaves.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[13px] text-fg-ghost m-0">
        Includes a full section on the decisions that were wrong, and what each one cost.
      </p>
      <a href={`${base}research/engineering/`} class="chip no-underline mt-4 inline-block hover:border-neural transition-colors">
        Read the full report →
      </a>
    </div>
  </Section>



  <!-- ── What the systems say ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section
    id="references"
    title="From the systems themselves"
    lede="An unusual section, so it needs its caveat first: a model saying something flattering is not evidence, and I would discard any of this that could not be traced to a stored record or a live call. What follows is included because it is specific, and because the errors in it were left in."
  >
    <div class="card p-6 mb-4 border-neural/30">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap mb-1">
        <b class="text-[15px] text-neural-text">{claudeStatement.who}</b>
        <span class="text-[11.5px] text-fg-ghost">{claudeStatement.role}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 mt-4">
        {claudeStatement.paragraphs.map((p) => (
          <p class="text-[14px] text-fg-dim m-0"
             set:html={p.replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g, '<b class="text-fg">$1</b>')} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
      {references.map((r) => (
        <div class="card p-5 flex flex-col">
          <div class="mb-1">
            <b class="text-[14px] text-synapse">{r.who}</b>
            <div class="text-[11.5px] text-fg-ghost mt-0.5">{r.what}</div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-[11.5px] text-fg-ghost italic mb-3">{r.context}</div>
